WEBVTT

01:20.080 --> 01:21.832
Ever since we...

01:24.584 --> 01:27.337
You're the only person
that I've ever...

01:28.380 --> 01:30.881
Sorry, this is weird.
I-I don't talk like this.

01:30.882 --> 01:32.509
No, it's okay.

01:37.431 --> 01:41.560
I feel like I'm coming apart.

01:43.770 --> 01:47.316
I think about you
all the time, Nikki.

01:49.151 --> 01:51.111
I try not to...

01:52.696 --> 01:55.115
...you're in every song
I listen to.

01:56.283 --> 01:58.284
You were the only person
who was nice to me

01:58.285 --> 01:59.869
when I moved here.

01:59.870 --> 02:02.456
And at first,
I thought maybe you...

02:07.461 --> 02:11.173
Well, I realized who you are.

02:12.549 --> 02:16.302
And then, after Nana passed,
you were the one that called

02:16.303 --> 02:18.804
even when I didn't have
anything to say

02:18.805 --> 02:20.432
and we just sat there.

02:22.267 --> 02:24.143
So I keep telling myself,
"Don't tell her.

02:24.144 --> 02:25.394
"She's too good.

02:25.395 --> 02:28.440
And she'll... you'll lose her."

02:29.983 --> 02:32.861
But maybe you should know...

02:34.404 --> 02:36.490
...that I would choose you
over everything.

02:38.241 --> 02:39.617
Aw.

02:39.618 --> 02:41.202
- That's everything.
- No, no. Stop.

02:41.203 --> 02:43.662
- Okay, th-th-that was cringey.
- Oh, my God. I knew it.

02:43.663 --> 02:44.830
- Way too much.
- I-I'm so sorry.

02:44.831 --> 02:46.457
I thought that was sweet.

02:46.458 --> 02:47.917
- I thought it was gross.
- I-I should've...

02:47.918 --> 02:49.168
- Okay, this time I want you...
- No, I...

02:49.169 --> 02:50.544
I'm not doing it again, dude.

02:50.545 --> 02:52.004
- That was so embarrassing.
- Yeah, yeah.

02:52.005 --> 02:53.464
That would freak...
Th-Th-That freaked me out.

02:53.465 --> 02:54.840
Okay? Nikki would vomit.

02:54.841 --> 02:56.342
You told me to pour
my heart out.

02:56.343 --> 02:57.511
Do you know how vulnerable
I just got?

02:58.345 --> 02:59.845
I underestimated you.

02:59.846 --> 03:01.555
What if you got her
something nice? -IAN: No, no.

03:01.556 --> 03:02.973
- I'll try that.
- D-Don't get her anything.

03:02.974 --> 03:04.141
Dude, you got to be less...

03:04.142 --> 03:06.394
way less sappy with Nikki, okay?

03:06.395 --> 03:07.895
She doesn't like that shit.
She doesn't.

03:07.896 --> 03:11.357
Flowers, the candy
that she said she likes?

03:11.358 --> 03:12.942
Okay.

03:12.943 --> 03:14.402
Thank you.

03:14.403 --> 03:15.986
What?

03:15.987 --> 03:17.071
Thank you.

03:17.072 --> 03:18.739
You want me to go?

03:18.740 --> 03:20.366
- Yeah, if-if you want, yeah.
- Oh, yeah, okay. Yeah.

03:20.367 --> 03:22.076
I'm sorry that...
I'm sorry I made you do that.

03:22.077 --> 03:23.369
No. No, it's okay. You're okay.

03:23.370 --> 03:24.703
- No, it-it just...
- It's a fun break.

03:24.704 --> 03:26.205
- Just pretend like...
- You're good.

03:26.206 --> 03:29.834
Oh, my God, dude,
that was so embarrassing.

03:29.835 --> 03:31.419
Can we leave?

03:31.420 --> 03:33.879
Yeah, well, thank God I did it.
That was... that was awful.

03:33.880 --> 03:35.548
Thank you for that.

03:35.549 --> 03:38.218
Have you ever actually, like,
flirted with Nikki?

03:39.010 --> 03:40.387
Invite romance.

03:41.221 --> 03:43.848
- Invite romance?
- Tease her.

03:43.849 --> 03:46.058
- Be playfully mean with her.
- Be mean to her?

03:46.059 --> 03:48.644
Playfully mean, yeah,
but bring up Freaky Nikki.

03:48.645 --> 03:50.354
You want me to call her
Freaky Nikki?

03:50.355 --> 03:51.856
You know she's sensitive
about that.

03:51.857 --> 03:53.315
Be like, "Hey, remember when
you used to get bullied?

03:53.316 --> 03:55.401
Everybody called you
Freaky Nikki?"

03:55.402 --> 03:56.902
She'll be like, "Oh, my God.

03:56.903 --> 03:59.113
"Oh, no, Bear, that was...
that was so long ago.

03:59.114 --> 04:00.699
Don't. Please."

04:01.450 --> 04:04.118
And that will, like,
take her breath away?

04:04.119 --> 04:06.579
Just say,

04:06.580 --> 04:09.457
"Nikki, I think we should grab
a drink sometime."

04:09.458 --> 04:10.624
Yeah, I've grabbed drinks
sometimes.

04:10.625 --> 04:12.084
She always invites you.

04:12.085 --> 04:13.461
- Yeah, exactly.
- I asked you guys not to come

04:13.462 --> 04:15.004
to trivia for one night.

04:15.005 --> 04:16.714
Y-You can't ask her out
at trivia, Bear.

04:16.715 --> 04:18.340
You can't.
I-I'm not gonna let you.

04:18.341 --> 04:20.134
It's a good,
organic time to ask.

04:20.135 --> 04:21.760
I love trivia night.

04:21.761 --> 04:22.678
It's all I have.

04:22.679 --> 04:24.597
I wake up every Wednesday

04:24.598 --> 04:26.056
rock hard,
thinking about trivia.

04:26.057 --> 04:28.434
God, I can't get over
how dumb I just looked.

04:28.435 --> 04:29.894
Y-You can't turn
our weekly gathering

04:29.895 --> 04:31.687
of camaraderie and skill
i-into your... your...

04:31.688 --> 04:33.647
your seven-year-late
promposal, Bear.

04:33.648 --> 04:35.941
Then when do I ask?

04:35.942 --> 04:37.985
Any other time.

04:37.986 --> 04:39.945
All you have is time.

04:42.616 --> 04:44.617
If she means this much to you--

04:44.618 --> 04:48.287
and I know she does-- wait.

04:48.288 --> 04:49.956
Do it at the right time.

04:51.249 --> 04:52.834
Okay.

04:54.878 --> 04:56.003
Okay, I'll wait.

04:56.004 --> 04:58.006
- I'll do it right.
- Now say it with me.

04:59.090 --> 05:01.675
All you have is time.

05:07.307 --> 05:08.767
Oh, no.

05:09.976 --> 05:11.561
Sandy?

05:13.438 --> 05:14.688
Sandy?

05:19.819 --> 05:21.571
Oh, no.

05:22.822 --> 05:24.658
Sandy?

05:26.076 --> 05:27.660
No.

05:27.661 --> 05:29.621
No, no, no, no.

05:30.664 --> 05:33.165
Oh, no, no. No, no!

05:33.166 --> 05:35.377
Oh, shit.

05:36.586 --> 05:39.047
How did you get into these?

05:41.049 --> 05:42.926
Oh, man.

06:13.039 --> 06:14.916
Why can't she...

06:16.167 --> 06:17.752
Just...

06:42.652 --> 06:44.695
- Hey.
- Wow, you are so lucky.

06:44.696 --> 06:47.072
Today was so busy.

06:47.073 --> 06:48.407
Oh.

06:48.408 --> 06:49.992
I needed a good day off.

06:49.993 --> 06:51.744
Oh, yeah. Definitely.

06:51.745 --> 06:55.080
You work so hard.

06:55.081 --> 06:56.332
You know I do.

06:56.333 --> 06:57.916
Oh, uh, what time are you
showing up tonight?

06:57.917 --> 07:00.127
I want to secure the spot early.

07:00.128 --> 07:01.713
Oh.

07:02.631 --> 07:04.674
Um, I'll...

07:07.052 --> 07:10.471
I don't think I'm gonna
make it tonight, actually.

07:10.472 --> 07:12.306
Aw, Bear, no.

07:12.307 --> 07:13.766
I wanted to see you tonight.

07:13.767 --> 07:15.100
We need your brain.

07:15.101 --> 07:16.644
We got to beat
the Rag Tags this week.

07:16.645 --> 07:18.897
Uh, well, I mean...

07:19.939 --> 07:21.524
I...

07:22.692 --> 07:24.443
I-I don't...
I don't think I can tonight.

07:24.444 --> 07:26.905
I'm just catching up
on some stuff.

07:28.782 --> 07:31.867
I was gonna tell you something.

07:31.868 --> 07:33.202
What?

07:33.203 --> 07:35.120
I mean, should I, like,
tell you now?

07:35.121 --> 07:36.623
Yeah.

07:37.415 --> 07:38.958
What?

07:41.961 --> 07:45.674
Yeah, so I'm putting in
my two weeks.

07:47.884 --> 07:49.177
Really?

07:53.473 --> 07:54.974
How come?

07:57.310 --> 07:59.269
I don't know.

07:59.270 --> 08:03.315
Yeah, we're kind of running
out of time, Bear, so, um...

08:03.316 --> 08:05.567
you know,
might want to skip that stuff

08:05.568 --> 08:07.528
you're working on.

08:07.529 --> 08:09.488
You're right.

08:09.489 --> 08:11.156
- Tonight's the night.
- Shit!

08:11.157 --> 08:12.408
Goddamn it!

08:12.409 --> 08:13.951
Are you okay?

08:13.952 --> 08:16.495
No, I just dropped my crystal
necklace down the drain.

08:16.496 --> 08:18.997
- Oh, shit.
- Ugh!

08:18.998 --> 08:20.542
Sorry.

08:22.877 --> 08:24.795
Why would she even say that?

08:24.796 --> 08:26.088
Hey, uh, we're closing soon,

08:26.089 --> 08:27.798
so let me know
if you need anything.

08:27.799 --> 08:29.049
Oh, o-okay.

08:29.050 --> 08:30.718
- Thank you.
- Right. Yeah, I know.

08:30.719 --> 08:32.344
Ryan was saying that, too,
so I'm not the only one.

08:32.345 --> 08:33.846
Oh, you're
definitely not the only one.

08:33.847 --> 08:35.556
- I know.
- Hey, uh, sorry.

08:35.557 --> 08:36.890
I-I do need help.

08:36.891 --> 08:39.727
Um, do you have, uh,
crystal necklaces?

08:39.728 --> 08:41.812
Yeah. Yeah, here,
let me show you.

08:41.813 --> 08:43.689
No, honestly, 'cause that's
what I was saying before.

08:43.690 --> 08:45.859
Like, what? What are you
even talking about?

08:49.696 --> 08:51.363
Oh, my God, that's crazy.

08:51.364 --> 08:52.656
- What?
- No.

08:52.657 --> 08:53.866
Hold on a second.

08:53.867 --> 08:55.367
Um, so this is all we have.

08:55.368 --> 08:57.202
Yeah, each rock has its own

08:57.203 --> 08:59.872
kind of unique energy
and whatever.

08:59.873 --> 09:01.915
So, the amethyst is for
calmness, clarity,

09:01.916 --> 09:04.585
and then the rose quartz
attracts, like, love and shit.

09:04.586 --> 09:08.422
What's one that's, like, good...

09:08.423 --> 09:10.758
energy or, like, good vibes?

09:10.759 --> 09:12.760
Probably the citrine.

09:12.761 --> 09:16.054
I mean, it's basically
sunshine in a rock.

09:16.055 --> 09:17.765
Okay. Thanks.

09:17.766 --> 09:20.101
Yeah. Let me know
if you need anything else.

09:20.894 --> 09:22.519
Sunshine in a rock.

09:22.520 --> 09:23.896
Well, no,
'cause yesterday at lunch,

09:23.897 --> 09:25.814
Becca was being, like,
such a... Yeah.

09:25.815 --> 09:27.817
Nikki would hate that.

09:28.943 --> 09:31.029
No, that's what I'm saying.

09:33.531 --> 09:34.907
And then her bringing Ryan
with her?

09:34.908 --> 09:37.284
I was like,
"What are you even doing?"

09:41.581 --> 09:42.664
Like, really?

09:42.665 --> 09:44.584
You know we don't even like him.

09:46.252 --> 09:47.962
Just so annoying.

09:50.173 --> 09:51.633
Yeah.

09:54.093 --> 09:56.303
Honestly, 'cause that's what
I was saying...

10:08.817 --> 10:11.318
What, no crystal?

10:11.319 --> 10:13.070
I like this.

10:13.071 --> 10:15.906
Yeah, well, they've been pretty
popular since we put them out.

10:15.907 --> 10:17.992
You know,
everybody wants a wish.

10:21.037 --> 10:23.622
Well, it's not for me, so...

10:23.623 --> 10:26.792
Okay, well, don't come back
complaining.

10:26.793 --> 10:28.377
Do people complain
about these or...?

10:28.378 --> 10:30.379
Well, they're kind of like
collectibles,

10:30.380 --> 10:33.048
so some people don't open them,
but the people who do,

10:33.049 --> 10:35.635
you know, come back
and complain.

10:39.305 --> 10:40.973
'Cause it's a scam or...?

10:40.974 --> 10:42.975
Hey, man, we're not
scammers, okay?

10:42.976 --> 10:44.309
No, no, I don't mean
that you're a scammer,

10:44.310 --> 10:46.436
but just, like,
why do they complain?

10:46.437 --> 10:49.147
'Cause they're mad

10:49.148 --> 10:51.066
- 'cause it doesn't work?
- Yeah, or whatever.

10:51.067 --> 10:54.820
Or it does work and
it, like, ruins their lives?

10:54.821 --> 10:56.530
Or they die
or wish they were dead.

10:59.909 --> 11:01.243
You're good, very good.

11:01.244 --> 11:03.078
Yeah, you could write a review.

11:03.079 --> 11:04.997
This is gonna be seven...

11:04.998 --> 11:07.457
Have you ever even been
into a Guitar Center?

11:07.458 --> 11:09.042
- No.
- They aren't all tuned.

11:09.043 --> 11:10.544
- So, basically...
- It's not about the guitars,

11:10.545 --> 11:12.296
- and you know that.
- Those teenagers are fucking

11:12.297 --> 11:14.006
slapping it like a bass,
and the shitty demo strings--

11:14.007 --> 11:15.465
- don't even get me started.
- Ladies, please.

11:15.466 --> 11:17.092
He doesn't expect them
to be tuned all the time.

11:17.093 --> 11:18.510
It's...

11:18.511 --> 11:20.053
If you're working
on your book or whatever...

11:20.054 --> 11:21.555
- Girls.
- ...or you're on the clock,

11:21.556 --> 11:23.181
it would give you
something to do. -Oh, my God.

11:23.182 --> 11:24.683
I never work on my book
when there are customers

11:24.684 --> 11:26.226
in the store,
so why does it matter?

11:26.227 --> 11:27.936
I know, but look, I'm the one
that has to go home

11:27.937 --> 11:30.856
and hear my dad complain
about my friends all night.

11:30.857 --> 11:32.274
I'm just asking you to pretend

11:32.275 --> 11:34.192
- like you're working.
- What?

11:34.193 --> 11:35.694
- Just, like...
- I mean, it's easy

11:35.695 --> 11:37.029
- for you to say...
- No.

11:37.030 --> 11:38.614
...when you're leaving
for tattoo school.

11:38.615 --> 11:41.199
It's art school,
and I haven't gotten in yet.

11:41.200 --> 11:42.743
I thought you got into Luther.

11:42.744 --> 11:44.328
No, I said
I want to go to Luther.

11:44.329 --> 11:46.204
- Sorry, I didn't...
- Still have a shot.

11:46.205 --> 11:47.664
- Good. -SARAH: Sorry.
- Later.

11:47.665 --> 11:49.458
I-I just don't want you
to get in trouble. -Later.

11:49.459 --> 11:50.918
I know, babe.
I love you. -SARAH: I love you.

11:50.919 --> 11:52.836
What the fuck
are you guys doing?

11:52.837 --> 11:55.005
- Uh...
- Ian's just messing with me.

11:55.006 --> 11:57.466
I look over, and these two
are just...

11:58.593 --> 12:00.344
Hey, cut the shit.

12:00.345 --> 12:02.471
Hey, can we focus up? This is,
uh, this is very serious to me.

12:02.472 --> 12:03.972
I'm gonna go get some shots.

12:03.973 --> 12:05.140
- Great idea, Nikki.
- I'll-I'll come with you.

12:05.141 --> 12:06.683
Thank you. Thank you.

12:06.684 --> 12:08.769
What the fuck
were you guys doing?

12:08.770 --> 12:10.062
After.

12:10.063 --> 12:11.855
Four shots of tequila, please.

12:11.856 --> 12:13.440
Um, and anything else?

12:13.441 --> 12:15.026
I'll get a piña colada.

12:16.402 --> 12:18.070
A piña colada?

12:18.071 --> 12:20.155
Don't make fun of my drink.

12:20.156 --> 12:21.573
- What?
- I like a man

12:21.574 --> 12:24.409
who's in touch
with his feminine side.

12:24.410 --> 12:25.911
- Why is that feminine?
- It's not.

12:25.912 --> 12:27.245
I don't like the taste
of the alcohol.

12:27.246 --> 12:30.124
- Yeah, we'll get you juice.
- Wow.

12:30.917 --> 12:32.376
Wait, so what was
the important stuff

12:32.377 --> 12:34.461
- on the phone today?
- A lot.

12:34.462 --> 12:36.046
I did a lot of really
important things.

12:36.047 --> 12:38.090
- That?
- Cleaned.

12:38.091 --> 12:40.842
- Mm.
- I did my taxes.

12:40.843 --> 12:43.053
- I did...
- You watched TV all day.

12:43.054 --> 12:45.305
Yeah, that's all I did.

12:45.306 --> 12:46.807
Bear.

12:46.808 --> 12:48.309
Yeah.

12:50.436 --> 12:52.229
So, uh, I was thinking...

12:52.230 --> 12:53.772
Got a card for the shots?

12:53.773 --> 12:55.273
Uh, yes.

12:55.274 --> 12:56.400
I got it.

12:56.401 --> 12:57.859
Okay, fine. Yes.

12:57.860 --> 13:00.278
You can... But I think...

13:00.279 --> 13:01.905
- Ah.
- I said I got it.

13:01.906 --> 13:04.033
Yeah, you got to be
quicker than that.

13:04.784 --> 13:05.867
Thank you.

13:05.868 --> 13:07.370
You're welcome.

13:08.579 --> 13:10.248
Uh...

13:11.040 --> 13:12.791
Anyway, um...

13:12.792 --> 13:14.835
- I went to the store...
- Open or closed?

13:14.836 --> 13:16.879
Oh. Open, babe.

13:18.715 --> 13:20.007
I was just trying
to say that I...

13:20.008 --> 13:21.383
you said you dropped
your necklace...

13:21.384 --> 13:23.343
Guys, Sarah just told me
that her dad keeps a gun

13:23.344 --> 13:25.303
- in the break room safe.
- Wow.

13:25.304 --> 13:26.722
Are you serious?

13:26.723 --> 13:27.889
Dead serious.

13:27.890 --> 13:29.141
I feel like he, like,

13:29.142 --> 13:30.350
should've mentioned that
or something.

13:30.351 --> 13:32.144
Not if it's locked away.
It's fine.

13:32.145 --> 13:34.855
Oh, my God, I'm so sorry.
Um, you were saying something.

13:34.856 --> 13:36.857
Yeah, what were you saying?

13:36.858 --> 13:38.650
I was just saying,

13:38.651 --> 13:41.236
um, I... I'll just...
I'll tell you later.

13:41.237 --> 13:42.904
It's fine. I-I got...
I went to this...

13:42.905 --> 13:45.323
Didn't realize we were all
taking a field trip to the bar.

13:45.324 --> 13:47.034
- Ooh la la.
- All right.

13:47.035 --> 13:49.870
- To... Okay.
- Fine, yeah.

13:49.871 --> 13:52.039
What are we cheers-ing to?

13:52.040 --> 13:53.665
To Sandy.

13:53.666 --> 13:55.333
Thanks for coming out
tonight. -NIKKI and IAN: Oh.

13:55.334 --> 13:57.335
- It is trivia time.
- Mm-mm. All right.

13:57.336 --> 13:59.588
- And as always...
- Let's get these fuckers, huh?

13:59.589 --> 14:01.631
All right. -Yeah,
I'm looking at you, bitch.

14:01.632 --> 14:03.759
- Here we go.
- ...will win a $100 Visa.

14:03.760 --> 14:06.470
Why to Sandy?

14:06.471 --> 14:08.472
She died. -HOST: And tonight's
theme is going to be...

14:08.473 --> 14:10.640
- What?
- ...early film trivia.

14:10.641 --> 14:12.059
Sandy died.

14:12.060 --> 14:13.477
Okay, this first one's
a two-parter...

14:13.478 --> 14:14.936
- What?
- Yeah.

14:14.937 --> 14:16.855
...and you have to
answer both. Here we go.

14:16.856 --> 14:18.273
Really?

14:18.274 --> 14:20.442
This animated film
features a blue genie

14:20.443 --> 14:22.069
- that can grant three wishes.
- Bear, I'm so sorry.

14:22.070 --> 14:23.361
Oh, it's okay.

14:23.362 --> 14:25.113
What is the name
of this movie...?

14:25.114 --> 14:26.364
Guys, settle down.

14:26.365 --> 14:27.866
- Bear.
- Settle down.

14:27.867 --> 14:29.201
Okay, okay, guys...

14:29.202 --> 14:30.869
Come on, douchebags.
We're going to Greedo's.

14:30.870 --> 14:33.371
No, please.
I just want to go home.

14:33.372 --> 14:35.123
You're saying no to karaoke?

14:35.124 --> 14:37.918
I'm saying no to bad singers
and sticky tabletops

14:37.919 --> 14:40.003
when I just want
to go home and sleep.

14:40.004 --> 14:41.213
All right, so who's gonna dance

14:41.214 --> 14:42.464
when I "Slim Shady"
the whole joint?

14:42.465 --> 14:44.091
"Who's gonna dance when I

